{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And YHWH descended upon Mount Sinai.</b> The language of 'descent' in reference to the Holy One, blessed be He, is in every instance a matter of His showing Himself and being revealed in the apprehension of the intellect. It is like the expression (Genesis 18:1), ״וירא אליו ה'״ — 'and YHWH appeared to him' — said of Abraham; and thus Onkelos translated it ואתגלי, 'and He was revealed,' just as he translated וירא. But Scripture employed the language of descent because a revelation of the Shekhinah to those below constitutes a descent relative to the exalted heights. And the meaning of 'and YHWH descended' here is that YHWH, the distinctive Name, appeared before the eyes of all the people, for so it stated above: ״כי ביום השלישי ירד ה' לעיני כל העם״ — 'for on the third day YHWH will descend before the eyes of all the people.' For through their seeing the Glory as a consuming fire on the top of the mountain, they knew and understood that there was the distinctive Name of YHWH; and to this intent 'and YHWH descended' was said — not that they saw the distinctive Name of YHWH itself, for it is written (Exodus 33:20): ״כי לא יראני האדם וחי״ — 'for no man shall see Me and live.' And so too the matter with Abraham: the statement ״וירא אליו ה'״ declares that the distinctive Name of YHWH appeared to Abraham, yet it is already well known that the Patriarchs did not apprehend the distinctive Name, nor did He appear to them except through El Shaddai, which is the gateway to YHWH. Therefore Scripture needed to say ״והוא יושב פתח האהל״ — 'and he was sitting at the entrance of the tent' — which clarifies the וירא אליו: Scripture thereby teaches you that His appearing to Abraham was through the opening of the tent, so that you should not understand that the distinctive Name of YHWH appeared to him in actuality. And so here, in 'and YHWH descended,' it is equivalent — for the revelation of the distinctive Name of YHWH before the eyes of all the people was through the appearance of the Glory, which they saw as a consuming fire."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:15.995578552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}